#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Upgrade a verified DwemerDistro from Debian 12 (Bookworm) to Debian 13 (Trixie).

Root only. Only the Launcher's OS maintenance runs it; update.sh installs it but never runs it.

  status    [--json]  Report the upgrade state. Reads files only; changes nothing.
  preflight [--json]  Check the layout and rehearse the APT solution against the signed Trixie
                      suites in a private APT directory. Downloads packages; changes no system state.
                      A stopped PG17 (a reopened distro) is proven to be the journaled cluster
                      offline, inspected on a private socket only and stopped again.
  upgrade --prepare --plan-id ID
                      Fence writers (Apache, PHP-FPM, PostgreSQL) and issue a capture token. The
                      Launcher then terminates the distro and exports and verifies a recovery copy.
  upgrade --capture-token TOKEN --recovery-sha256 HEX --recovery-bytes N
                      Run (or resume) the upgrade against that verified recovery copy.
  upgrade --cancel    Release the fence before any package changed.
  verify    [--json]  After the distro restarted: verify the upgraded system privately. The fence
                      stays; no application may write yet.
  release   [--json]  After a successful verify, once the Launcher has durably recorded that it will
                      no longer roll back automatically: open the system for writes. Repeatable.

Exit codes: 0 done; 1 failed (see the log); 2 usage; 3 deferred, nothing changed; 4 restart the
distro, then verify again; 75 another maintenance operation is running, nothing changed.
"""

